    "rationale": "Four internal nodes (12,13,15,16) are shifted vertically to exploit the vacancy hotspot at y=25–26 (window_21_27_24_30 and window_21_27_23_29) and reduce congestion around y=27–30. Node 12 moves down 1 tile to y=25, aligning with its neighbor median [24,24] and shortening edges [10,12], [11,12], [12,15]. Nodes 13 and 15 move down 1 tile to y=26, eliminating the detour on edge [12,15] (steps drop from 7→5) and freeing space near x=22–24. Node 16 moves down 1 tile to y=29, preserving fanout to 3 while avoiding overlap with 13/15 and enabling shorter route to output. The bounding box remains min_x=20, max_x=28, min_y=20, max_y=35 (area=144), but internal wire density drops and routing feasibility improves—critical since prior height-16 layouts failed routing when vertical spacing was tight. All moves are collision-free and respect dependency layers."
